#{[17592186055837 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055837 #edb/ref 1061 607420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055837 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b81ec1ae-2147-51bf-abd0-42837ec9335a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055837 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055838 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055838 #edb/ref 1061 607421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055838 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a86683d5-cc60-54e3-a1ca-8ddc210beec5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055838 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055839 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055839 #edb/ref 1061 607422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055839 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "708e4952-07a2-52aa-83ee-e86a33ffcc1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055839 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055840 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055840 #edb/ref 1061 607425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055840 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b4fa400d-ccbf-5b93-8bb2-f08b681dc5d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055840 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055841 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055841 #edb/ref 1061 607428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055841 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5dc0ae8-3ca8-53a2-a100-962fd53b4781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055841 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055842 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055843 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055842 #edb/ref 1061 607431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055842 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3caa8c6c-0602-56f3-a037-3db5c98ff22b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055842 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186055958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055843 #edb/ref 1061 607432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055843 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e7a9127a-071f-5089-a135-f41568b6862d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055843 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055942 #edb/ref 1064 "The **Cartesian coordinate system** (or **Cartesian plane**) is a grid that we can use to understand where certain objects lie, similar to a map. This grid looks as follows:\n\n![](images/fd/fd702a53ff1127a2432cbdd9a3c7057a08c73ac7a086454c066fa2c96bea7974.png)\n\nIt consists of a horizontal number line called the **$x$-axis** and a vertical number line called the **$y$-axis**.\n\nThe **origin** is the location where the $x$ and $y$ axes meet and is given the symbol $O.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055942 #edb/ref 1065 1431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055942 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "dacc8373-6186-517b-bba8-ec1729732e4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055942 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055943 #edb/ref 1064 "Every location on the Cartesian plane is called a **point**. Every point is identified using an $x$**-coordinate** and a $y$**-coordinate**. Together, points are expressed using an **ordered pair** of **coordinates** $(x,y).$\n\nFor example, we can mark (or **plot**) the point $A$ with coordinates $({\\color{red}{3}},{\\color{blue}{2}})$ by starting from $O$ and then traveling $\\color{red}3$ units towards the right, followed $\\color{blue}2$ units up.\n\n![](images/c1/c1ef61dedbbcc6eedcd125c2c62cdfbaa4d9b9a12f10181714b51c060a059fd3.png)\n\nWe say that\n\n- the $x$-coordinate of $A$ is $3$,\n\n- the $y$-coordinate of $A$ is $2$,\n\n- the $xy$-coordinates (or just \"the coordinates\") of $A$ are $(3,2).$\n\nThe letter $A$ is just a label for our point. It's usually a good idea to label points!" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055943 #edb/ref 1065 1432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055943 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9e7847c5-757a-5cb8-b947-9c7d806b5dc5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055943 #edb/ref 1067 "Coordinates and Ordered Pairs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055957 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that a coordinate plane is made by two number lines that meet at $0.$ Since these are number lines, we can extend both to include negative numbers.\n\n![](images/f1/f1eeb7f3bc0ab8b39e9dc7127d76a32f1dd130d380748fedc6e11b967f3878ed.png)\n\nWe plot an ordered pair $({\\color{red}x},{\\color{blue}y})$ similar to before, but if the number is negative, we reverse the direction. So, starting at the origin:\n\n- if the first number is positive, move that number of places *right* along the $\\color{red}x$-axis. If its negative, move *left*.\n\n- if the second number is positive, move that number of places *up* along the $\\color{blue}y$-axis. If its negative, move *down*.\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find the coordinates of the point $Q$ above.\n\nTo find the coordinates of $Q,$ we start at the origin, move $\\color{red}3$ units *left*, and then $\\color{blue}2$ units *down*. \n\n![](images/b4/b4f58f0c1ad6dc2936ed1b24c844fa82c1b1d5ec10c80e14c6a43f6f4eaf5544.png)\n\nSince we move left, the $\\color{red}x$-coordinate is negative, and since we move down, the $\\color{blue}y$-coordinate is negative.\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of $Q$ are $({\\color{red}{-3}},{\\color{blue}{-2}}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055957 #edb/ref 1065 2092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055957 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7383452c-9470-5f05-b206-dffbb84808dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055957 #edb/ref 1067 "Extending the Coordinate Plane to Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055958 #edb/ref 1064 "The axes split the coordinate plane into four parts, called **quadrants**.\n\n![](images/93/938125e855fcb96f743c01f2a00d289ef13e0601772bab56cf0f255e9adf4dcd.png)\n\nGoing counter-clockwise, it's common to call\n\n- the top-right quadrant the first quadrant (I),\n\n- the top-left is the second quadrant (II),\n\n- the bottom-left is the third quadrant (III),\n\n- and and bottom-right is the fourth quadrant (IV).\n\nTo remember the order of the quadrants, it's helpful to think about writing the letter \"C\" in the graph:\n\n![](images/1e/1ef91f2bc25ea8b887ec449d2dafe2eaf6a157733e7bc50e4480280df8190728.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055958 #edb/ref 1065 2097 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055958 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8a1e27dd-9f87-5adf-b0c6-f0f6cd7e2aac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055958 #edb/ref 1067 "Quadrants in the Coordinate Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056014 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we wish to find the equation of the **horizontal line** that passes through the point $(0,3)$, as shown below:\n\n![](images/37/379af2ba930fa537f1fbdda5b4b5cc91e355a46e90918cdc56bbce66f3502d7b.png)\n\nNotice that for *any* $x$-value on the line, the $y$-value is always $\\color{red}3.$ \n\n![](images/ff/ff5ec246a558fc981ba5f0b0085ce3663ac6ab837121f31a5d44de6adb91cb90.png)\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is $y=3.$\n\n**Note**: When writing the equation of a horizontal line, we always put the variable $y$ on the left side and the constant on the right side." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056014 #edb/ref 1065 8070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056014 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8d036bf9-1cb2-59e4-a418-b586ec35d56e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056014 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056015 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to find the equation of the **vertical line** that passes through the point $(-4,0)$, as shown below:\n\n![](images/06/065dfc149c1624bbe2c6fd51085c48b5e60c1d37d248d073dd1374d08e65b5af.png)\n\nNotice that for *any* $y$-value on the line, the $x$-value is always $\\color{red}-4.$ \n\n![](images/01/01d24274cc3d2b5a7899cc1aa8cee4aef4fb02ddb45acd27629a57d6af41a398.png)\n\nTherefore, the equation of this vertical line is $x=-4.$\n\n**Note**: When writing the equation of a vertical line, we always put the variable $x$ on the left side and the constant on the right side." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056015 #edb/ref 1065 8071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056015 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "fcdbdf94-22ce-5781-9f56-42dc93763172" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056015 #edb/ref 1067 "Vertical Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186066977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186066978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186066979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186066980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186066981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186066981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066976 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "3f04668a-3df1-560e-950f-53985118bf87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066977 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066977 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066977 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "88eabd55-766f-573b-8305-9db9fb46fea2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066978 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066978 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066978 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b827aac1-596d-54de-9317-02f420f5b264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066979 #edb/ref 1080 "5\\sqrt{13}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066979 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066979 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dc9efbb1-7d26-572a-8d2c-c509a6d4a218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066980 #edb/ref 1080 "8\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066980 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066980 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f4a39913-c29c-5674-8ad9-5afeccfbe7b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066981 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{65}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066981 #edb/